Playwright visual regression rules. See the `Visual test rules` section of [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) for the canonical guide.

- Baselines are stored at `tests/visual/stories.spec.ts-snapshots/<story-id>-chromium-linux.png` and must be generated on Linux to match CI.
- After adding / renaming / changing a story, regenerate baselines via the Playwright Linux container:
  ```bash
  docker run --rm --ipc=host -e CI=true -v "$(pwd)":/work -w /work \
    mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.59.1-noble bash -lc \
    "npm i -g pnpm@11.5.0 >/dev/null && pnpm install --frozen-lockfile && \
     pnpm run build-storybook && pnpm run test:visual:update"
  ```
- Review the regenerated PNGs visually before committing. Never commit `-actual.png` / `-diff.png` outputs.
- Flake mitigation already in [playwright.config.ts](mdc:playwright.config.ts): fixed viewport (1280x800), `en-GB` locale, UTC timezone, light colour scheme, reduced-motion. Do not loosen `maxDiffPixelRatio` — stub non-determinism in the story instead.
- The spec reads `storybook-static/index.json`; stories must build (`pnpm run build-storybook`) before `pnpm run test:visual` runs.
